---
// Honest builder-vs-custom card. Shared by the landing comparison and the
// websites service page so the framing stays identical in both places.
---
<div data-reveal class="border border-[rgba(var(--line-rgb),0.14)] p-9 max-[760px]:p-6">
  <div class="font-semibold text-[11px] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] tracking-[.2em] text-[var(--accent-vis)] mb-4">THE HONEST TRADEOFF</div>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-12 gap-y-8 max-[760px]:grid-cols-1">
    <div>
      <h3 class="m-0 mb-2 font-extrabold text-[19px] font-['Archivo'] tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--ink0)]">Website builder</h3>
      <p class="m-0 font-normal text-[13.5px] leading-[1.65] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-[var(--ink3)]">You can drag-and-drop the layout around yourself, whenever you like. Total control, at the cost of speed, security and looking home-made.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="m-0 mb-2 font-extrabold text-[19px] font-['Archivo'] tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--ink0)]">A site from me</h3>
      <p class="m-0 font-normal text-[13.5px] leading-[1.65] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-[var(--ink3)]">The design lives in the code, so changing the layout means editing the code, which is my job. That constraint is the point: it is what makes the site load faster and gives your customers the best possible experience. You still edit your own content; the layout stays fast and professional.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
